  "interpretation": "In this satin-portrait prompt context, explicitly describing smooth drape, tension folds, and geometry-following specular reflections did not improve perceived material physics over naming satin alone. The material-physics variant scored 0.75 lower on the primary material_physics dimension and 0.125 lower overall, despite a 0.25 gain in aesthetic quality. This single small-N run contradicts the tested superiority hypothesis in this context, but it does not establish that explicit material-physics language is generally harmful. Replication across prompts, materials, lighting conditions, and routes is required before changing any general compiler rule.",
